{"title":"24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Twenty-four (written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />) is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integer</a> following <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Twenty-three\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Twenty-three\">twenty-three</a> and before <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Twenty-five&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Twenty-five (page does not exist)\">twenty-five</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Properties\">Properties</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Properties\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>It is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Composite\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Composite\">composite</a>; its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime_factorization\" title=\"Prime factorization\">prime factorization</a> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/9/ee9c21ae7a2b0fabb5dffb175ccd95ee100fd33b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3\\cdot3^1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" />.</li>\n<li>It cannot be written as the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Difference\" title=\"Difference\">difference</a> of two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perfect_square\" title=\"Perfect square\">perfect squares</a>.</li>\n<li>It is the dimension of the Leech lattice, a highly symmetrical lattice which is also the most efficient way to pack hyperspheres in its dimension.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">Integer</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_theory\" title=\"Number theory\">Number theory</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=24&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018071457\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.019 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 29/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 247/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 353/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.255      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.255      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:30860:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018071457 and revision id 242690. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}